{"agent":"bg112","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new test does not model two give-ups of one waiter, and its assertion cannot pass on a correct park-on-retry implementation. Inside the holder, round 0 times `patient` out, then starts a blocking `_waiter` named `patient` and waits until that ticket is queued. Round 1 then calls `SL.hold(..., \"patient\")` again while that waiter is still queued, starts `late1`, and starts a second blocking `_waiter` also named `patient`. Four acquirers are joined (`late0`, `patient`, `late1`, `patient`). After the holder releases, a correct queue yields `[\"patient\", \"late0\", \"late1\", \"patient\"]` (the first parked retry runs, then the two lates, then the extra same-name waiter), which fails `assert order == [\"patient\", \"late0\", \"late1\"]`. The second short `hold` is a concurrent same-name acquisition, not a retry after the first waiter has left the queue, so the “gives up twice and keeps the same place both times” claim is never exercised. The unfixed code also fails the assertion (four names, patient not stably first), so the test does not go red-then-green on B5225d3ad22.","digest":"fd8696c64f83c35b","family":"xai","location":"tests/test_suitelock_queue.py:155","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"tests/test_suitelock_queue.py:155"}],"chunks_total":1,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":1595,"diff_sha":"a2cef574fb18e343de728afc4055a014af527bb3833c226044548c66baf3d0e0","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B5225d3ad22","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":44.2,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"c24245adaa31f2ec","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B5225d3ad22.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261109T031657Z-dd88f070.jsonl","reason":"","review_degra