{"agent":"bg112","data":{"digest":"9f18f35c793808ec","finding":1,"gate":"rubber_duck","location":"tests/test_suitelock_queue.py:164","probe":"round 1 reuse: _Ticket.__init__ renaming the round-0 .parked back to .ticket happens BEFORE round-1's hold loop, so round-0's parked file cannot satisfy round-1's assert; a .parked exists after round 1 only if round-1's give-up parked it fresh (__exit__ self.park rename). Against the code at the bug's filing there is no .parked mechanism at all, so glob('*.parked') is empty and the round-0 assert fails already. And even a hypothetical 'parks once, drops the second' code fails round-1's assert, since the round-1 __init__ consumed the one parked file. The test is red on unfixed, green on fixed.","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_suitelock_queue.py:164","verdict":"refuted"},"id":"e1e12d65c9318745e29880465","kind":"review.triaged","lamport":158822,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B5225d3ad22","ts":"2026-11-09T03:23:06.171679Z"}
